# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_cochange_fairness.py" "CO-CHANGE FAIRNESS GATE: PASS" "co-change pool MULTI-TENANT FAIRNESS (per-tenant round-robin + per-account cap, mirroring the main event worker; P2-1)" "co-change pool FAIRNESS (audit finding P2-1): the MAIN event worker (event_queue.py _FairQueue) is multi-tenant FAIR -- per-account ROUND-ROBIN drain + a per-account cap (VERIPSA_PER_ACCOUNT_QUEUE_CAP) -- so one noisy tenant can neither starve nor crowd out the others. The dedicated CO-CHANGE pool (cochange.py) had NEITHER: it was a plain ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1), an UNBOUNDED strict-FIFO queue. A noisy tenant onboarding a big org (one populate_cochange_async per repo) or force-pushing a busy monorepo (one increment_cochange_async per push) piled slow blobless-clone tasks into the single FIFO ahead of EVERY other tenant -> a 2nd customer co-change (the ADVISORY 2nd signal) went stale until the noisy tenant clones finished. THE FIX gives the co-change pool the SAME mechanism by REUSING event_queue._FairQueue as its backlog store, drained by a single daemon worker (_CochangeScheduler) that KEEPS clone serialization (still max one task / one extra DB connection at a time -- no thread storm) but drains the BACKLOG per-account round-robin + caps each account slice (VERIPSA_PER_ACCOUNT_COCHANGE_CAP, env_int min_value=1, default 50 -- a bad knob fails LOUD at startup, never a silently-disabled path). Over the per-account cap the submit is DROPPED CONTENT-FREE + FAIL-OPEN: nothing enqueued, ONE content-free line logged (account = public GitHub owner id), a PRE-RESOLVED Future carrying a skipped marker returned (NEVER raises -- co-change is advisory, a dropped populate self-heals on the next push). The account key is resolved best-effort at SUBMIT time (gh.installation_account_id, the SAME stable tenant key the task pins by); a degraded gh whose resolution raises still gets a keyless fair bucket, never a crash -- and the AUTHORITATIVE fail-closed account resolution + cross-tenant guard still run INSIDE the task before any write, so the submit-time key only chooses the fair bucket, never routing. This gate proves it the way test_server.py proves the event worker fairness -- scheduler-level, DB-free + clone-free (deterministic, not a timing race): (a) ANTI-STARVATION -- tenant A floods 30 tasks, tenant B submits ONE last; under strict FIFO B is position 30, under fair round-robin B drains within the first couple (independent of A flood size); (b) PER-ACCOUNT CAP + DROP -- past the cap A further submits are dropped content-free (no raise, accepted bounded to the cap, the dropped Future still satisfies .result() with an advisory marker) while a DIFFERENT tenant submit is still accepted; (c) END-TO-END through the REAL dispatcher populate_cochange_async -- A over-cap onboards drop content-free + fail-open while B onboard is accepted and B task runs EARLY (not behind A flood), AND a degraded gh whose installation_account_id raises is still dispatched (never crashes onboarding); (d) the CAP KNOB is a validated env_int (min_value=1) so a 0/negative value is refused loudly at startup. Behaviour-preserving for the non-flooding case (single worker, same return shapes, same fail-open + content-free guarantees); only the BACKLOG order changes from FIFO to fair round-robin, plus the per-account cap. content-free throughout" "co-change pool fairness (P2-1): the dedicated co-change pool gets the main event worker per-tenant fairness -- _FairQueue REUSED as the backlog store (per-account round-robin + per-account cap VERIPSA_PER_ACCOUNT_COCHANGE_CAP) behind a single daemon worker that keeps clone serialization -- so a noisy tenant onboarding a big org / force-pushing a monorepo can no longer starve another tenant co-change; over-cap submits drop content-free + fail-open (never raise), account bucketed best-effort at submit time, content-free" 24
